// A2 vocabulary, grouped by theme.
//
// Each entry carries a present-tense sentence AND a Perfekt sentence, because
// Perfekt is where A2 learners actually struggle: it is not enough to know the
// word, you need to know whether it takes haben or sein and what the participle
// looks like. Nouns list their plural; verbs that take "sein" show it in the
// Perfekt example rather than being explained abstractly.
//
// Vocab themes are deliberately separate from the speaking themes in
// questions.js — there are far more of them here, and they need no questions.
//
// Adding your own: copy any line. Only `de`, `en`, `simple` and `perfekt` are
// required; `type` drives the little coloured tag.

